ralph/codex-output/iteration-000034-20260518-231202.log:1294:- Quota schema (0006_quota_policy_schema): a closed enum reused across tables is a Postgres DOMAIN over text + CHECK (here quota_resource over 14 dimensions, quota_enforcement_mode over hard/soft/metered/disabled); DROP DOMAIN goes in the down migration after the tables. quota_policies holds one limit per (scope, resource) where a row is EITHER a plan_default (text plan, no plans-table FK yet) OR an organization override — enforced by one table CHECK + two partial unique indexes; the checker resolves "org override else plan default". quota_usage is one counter row per (org, resource); quota_reservations are short-lived (amount>0, status active->committed|released|expired, expires_at, settled_at tied to non-active status by CHECK) and expose UNIQUE (organization_id, id) as a composite-FK target; usage_events is append-only (no updated_at/trigger, signed delta) and links reservations via a tenant-safe composite FK. An optional cross-table link inside a tenant uses a plain composite FK (MATCH SIMPLE) — NOT ON DELETE SET NULL, which would null the NOT NULL organization_id.
