ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:1214:- Real-quota concurrent oversubscription integration test (BE-0323 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/project_quota_concurrent_test.go; structural template for BE-0324..0338 — every other quota-dimension PRD story that needs to prove "parallel requests cannot oversubscribe the quota" against the dimension's owning Service.Create call): one Go test, t.Parallel, against testutil.RequireMigratedDB; wires a REAL *quota.Checker over a REAL *store.QuotaRepository + quota.StaticPlanResolver, and a REAL *store.<Resource>Service + REAL *store.AuditRepository, with the only fakes being the Authorizer and JobEnqueuer (recordingAuthorizer / recordingJobs from projectservice_test.go) which always succeed because their failure-path stories are covered elsewhere. Six load-bearing rules: (1) pre-seed quota_usage with used_value=0 for (org, dimension) BEFORE the race so the SELECT FOR UPDATE inside Checker.LockUsage acquires an existing row rather than racing inserts — the lock contract under test is row-lock serialisation, not row-creation; (2) seed quota_policies as scope_kind='plan_default' (not 'organization' override) so the plan-default fallback path inside QuotaRepository.EffectiveLimit is the one exercised — the org-override path has its own dedicated repository test (TestQuotaRepositoryEffectiveLimitPrefersOrgOverride); (3) launch attempts > limit goroutines (BE-0323 uses 20 attempts / limit 5 — 4:1 ratio gives a comfortable margin against any future pool-size or scheduling change without inflating runtime past ~0.5s); each goroutine generates its OWN canonical resource id via domain.MustNewID + a unique canonical slug fmt.Sprintf("p-%02d", i) so a slug conflict cannot disguise itself as a quota rejection; (4) assert successes == limit AND rejections == attempts - limit exactly, NOT >= / <= — the lock contract guarantees an exact split, and a "successes >= limit / <= attempts" range would silently let a regression through; (5) for EVERY rejection, assert all five ExceededDetail fields (Resource, Limit, Requested=1, Reserved==limit, Current==0) because at the moment the lock yields to a losing transaction every winning reservation is already committed — anything less than Reserved==limit means the lock did not serialise — and assert the diagnostic string never echoes any caller input (the i-indexed slug, display name, request id, or correlation id) so a future logging path cannot turn the error into a content channel; (6) post-race assertions cover three independent surfaces of the same invariant: raw count of projects rows for the org (must equal limit), raw count of active quota_reservations rows for the dimension (must equal limit), AND quotaRepo.SumActiveReservations through Store.Read (must equal limit) — the third surface catches a future regression where the table content diverges from the repository's view. Fake-call assertions pin step order at the unit-of-work level: authz.calls == attempts (every transaction reaches authorization) but jobs.calls == limit (rejected transactions never reach the JobEnqueuer because quota fails first and rolls back the whole tx). The dimension constant comes from the public store.QuotaResource* surface (BE-0323 uses store.QuotaResourceProjects) so a future rename surfaces as a compile error rather than a flaky test. NOT applicable to quota dimensions whose enforcement seam lives outside the *Service.Create unit of work (e.g. cpu_millicores / memory_mb / storage_gb where the dimension is summed across child resources — those need a different shape that exercises the dimension's actual enforcement gate). The CapDeploy concurrent_deployments dimension is the load-bearing precedent for "summed across rows" enforcement (DeploymentService.Create at deployment_service.go:209+691) and would clone this template by swapping the Service + dimension while keeping the six rules intact.
ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:8354:      "notes": "Quota dimension: services. BE-0325 services quota concurrent integration test added at internal/controlplane/store/service_quota_concurrent_test.go — clone of the BE-0324 structural template, covers AC4 (parallel requests cannot oversubscribe the services dimension); the other ACs are pinned by the existing serviceservice path (in-tx quota.Reserve at serviceservice.go:250 with QuotaResourceServices), envelope tests, and the redaction assertions inside the new test."
ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:8373:      "notes": "Quota dimension: applications (per-subtype). Service.Create now reserves TWO dimensions in the same DB transaction when Kind == ServiceKindApplication — the existing QuotaResourceServices reservation (BE-0325) and the new QuotaResourceApplications reservation. Non-application kinds (compose, database) do NOT consume the applications dimension. New integration tests at internal/controlplane/store/service_quota_applications_concurrent_test.go: (1) TestServiceServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionForApplicationsQuota — 20 goroutines × applications limit=5 with a loose services limit=40 prove the applications row lock serialises concurrent application creates; rejections carry ExceededDetail{Resource=applications,Limit=5,Requested=1,Reserved=5,Current=0}; service rows, active applications reservations, and active services reservations all == 5; (2) TestServiceServiceCreateAppliesApplicationsQuotaOnlyToApplicationKind — after exhausting the applications dimension with 5 application-kind services, a 6th application Create is rejected on applications while a compose-kind and a database-kind Create both succeed and only consume the services dimension. Pre-existing TestAPIKeyServiceCreate* and TestOrganizationVariableServicePatch* failures unchanged (factory id/slug-vs-ParseSlug issue documented under BE-0127 / BE-0324). gofmt, go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./..., and YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestServiceServiceCreate(Rejects|Applies)' ./internal/controlplane/store/ all pass."
ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:8430:      "notes": "Quota dimension: domains. ServiceDomainService.Create now reserves one unit on QuotaResourceDomains inside the same *Tx as the in-transaction authorize, the Insert, and the audit append (BE-0329). NewServiceDomainService gains a QuotaReserver dependency; cmd/yalla-api/main.go passes the existing serviceQuota placeholder until the real quota.Checker is wired into the HTTP layer. New integration tests at internal/controlplane/store/service_domain_quota_concurrent_test.go: (1) TestServiceDomainServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionForDomainsQuota — 20 goroutines x domains limit=5 prove the domains row lock serialises concurrent domain creates; rejections carry ExceededDetail{Resource=domains,Limit=5,Requested=1,Reserved=5,Current=0}; service_domains rows == 5; active domains reservations == 5; rejection diagnostic carries no caller hostname/request_id/correlation_id/domain_id leakage; (2) TestServiceDomainServiceCreateAppliesDomainsQuotaIndependentlyOfServicesQuota — after exhausting the domains dimension a 6th domain Create is rejected on the domains dimension and the services dimension is never touched (0 active services reservations). Pre-existing TestEnvironmentServiceCreateQuotaFailureRollsBack and TestOrganizationVariableServicePatchValueOnlyPreservesIsSecret failures unchanged (unrelated, documented under BE-0127 / BE-0324). gofmt, go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./..., and YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run \"TestServiceDomainServiceCreate(Rejects|Applies)\" ./internal/controlplane/store/ all pass."
ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:8449:      "notes": "Quota dimension: preview_environments. Implemented per-subtype Reserve(QuotaResourcePreviewEnvironments) on EnvironmentService.Create and Clone gated on Kind==EnvironmentKindPreview; added environments.kind column (migration 0025) with closed CHECK constraint (standard, preview) and partial index for the preview sweeper; CreateEnvironmentInput / CloneEnvironmentInput carry a new Kind field that normalises blank to EnvironmentKindStandard via validateEnvironmentKind so legacy callers stay green. Concurrent integration test (20 goroutines vs hard limit 5, services-dimension loose) and per-subtype boundary test (preview-exhausted but standard succeeds, blank-Kind normalises to standard) pass under go test and go test -race against a real Postgres."
ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:8544:      "notes": "Quota dimension: monthly_deployments. DeploymentService.Create and DeploymentService.Rollback both reserve monthly_deployments AFTER concurrent_deployments inside the same *Tx as the in-tx Authorize, the deployment row Insert, the provisioning-job Enqueue, and the audit Append — so a rejection on either dimension rolls the entire unit of work back. The constant QuotaResourceMonthlyDeployments and its DOMAIN membership were already in place from BE-0006 (migration 0006_quota_policy_schema.up.sql) and the in-source quota_internal_test.go count-equality guard, so no new migration was needed. Two new concurrent integration tests in internal/controlplane/store/deployment_quota_monthly_deployments_concurrent_test.go: RejectsParallelOversubscription (20 goroutines × monthly_deployments=5 → 5 successes, 15 typed CodeQuotaExceeded rejections whose ExceededDetail.Resource is monthly_deployments, Limit=5, Requested=1, Reserved=5, Current=0; rejection messages do not echo idempotency_key, request_id, correlation_id, or source_ref; deployments row count and active monthly_deployments reservations both equal 5; concurrent_deployments reservations stay at 0 because no policy is seeded for that dimension; SumActiveReservations agrees with raw count; authorizer.calls = 20 proves authorize ran on every attempt; jobs.calls = 5 proves enqueue ran only on winners, pinning the authorize→quota→insert→enqueue order under contention); AppliesIndependently (exhaust serially, sixth Create rejects on monthly_deployments specifically — never another dimension — and no concurrent_deployments or services reservation is ever taken)."
